        "original_id": "30ac46f1-ae84-5674-8452-3b05683ca404",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stanley Elkin, Anne Lamott, Jack Shoemaker\n- Works: Mrs. Ted Bliss\n- Companies: Hyperion Books\n- Topics: American consumerism, popular culture, male-female relations\n\nFacts:\n- Stanley Elkin was born on May 11, 1930, and he was an American novelist, short story writer, and essayist.\n- Anne Lamott was born on April 10, 1954, and she is an American novelist and non-fiction writer.\n- Stanley Elkin wrote extravagant, satirical fiction about American consumerism, popular culture, and male-female relations.\n- In 1995, Hyperion Books published Mrs. Ted Bliss, a novel by Stanley Elkin.\n- Stanley Elkin died on May 31, 1995.\n- Jack Shoemaker has published books by writers including Guy Davenport, Romulus Linney, Gary Snyder, Wendell Berry, Evan S. Connell, MFK Fisher, James Salter, Gina Berriault, Reynolds Price, W.S. Merwin, Michael Palmer, Donald Hall, Anne Lamott, Kay Boyle, Gary Nabhan, Jane Vandenburgh, Carole Maso, and Robert Aitken.",
